{
  "version": 27,
  "issued_at": "2026-08-09T00:00:00Z",
  "comment": "Policy 27. Points app_update at drawbridge 0.2.1 (version_code 12), which is v0.2.0 with android.permission.REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES removed from the manifest. That permission is what Play Protect reads when it refuses to let drawbridge install -- 'this app can install potentially harmful apps without your permission' -- and on 2026-08-08 it stopped a provisioned Moto G15 from updating itself at all, while herald, which declares nothing unusual, installed silently from the same installer. A Device Owner does not need it: verified on the provisioned emulator on 2026-08-09, where a DPC without the line still installed herald 6 -> 8 in place and herald mono from absent. required_apps is untouched, so no device re-fetches a browser. The url is pinned to the v0.2.1 tag rather than /releases/latest/download/ because v0.2.1 is published as a pre-release: it carries no herald assets, and making it 'latest' would 404 every required_apps URL on every device. Note the comment on policies 24 to 26 was never updated and still described policy 23.",
